      "content": "that sounds a lot better, thanks. i think the 'essential progress' part really sells it. \n\nactually, i'm a bit worried though. i got an email from a guy who owns a shop downtown and he's like, 'this is just a tax on the working class' and says it's going to kill small businesses. i don't want to make the newsletter look like we're ignoring them, but i also don't want to kill the vibe of the 'modern city' thing we just wrote. \n\ndo you think it's worth even mentioning the business concerns anymore, or would that just make the whole thing sound like a mess? is there a way to mention it without making it sound like the plan is flawed?",
